  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 119 AM CDT Thu Jul 30 2026\n\nAn expansive mid-level ridge will remain the dominant weather \nfeature through the period, though it will gradually retrograde \nfarther west this weekend and become centered over the lower \nColorado River Valley. This will allow slightly deeper moisture to\nreturn to South Texas and weaken the subsidence enough to support\nisolated showers and thunderstorms on Sunday, with rain chances \nincreasing to around 20-25% across much of the forecast area. \nDespite the uptick in rain chances, widespread wetting rainfall is\nnot anticipated.\n\nHot conditions will persist through the forecast period with daytime \nhighs generally in the upper 90s to around 105 degrees inland. While \nforecast heat indices have trended slightly lower for Saturday and \nSunday compared to previous forecasts, widespread values of 110+ \ndegrees remain likely, and Heat Advisories will probably be needed. \nHeat Risk continues to range from moderate to major with isolated \nareas of extreme remain possible through the weekend. Otherwise, \nlittle day-to-day change is expected as generally dry conditions \nprevail outside of isolated convection late in the weekend and early \nnext week.",
